<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Yield Spreads-Reverses narrowing.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Yield Spreads-Reverses narrowing.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> AUD VS   3-YR	   10-YR	* AUD 3-YR/10-YR SPREAD</p>
<p> USD	 78 (+ 03)   125 (+ 06) * FUTURES   97    (+ 06)</p>
<p> CAD	211 (+ 03)   143 (+ 10) * CASH	83    (+ 05)</p>
<p> NZD	-59 (- 04)   +04 (- 04) *</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Australian bonds reversed Thursday's narrowing trend in spread differentials to the U.S. and Canada as the market anticipated another sharp sell-off in U.S. Treasuries when its PPI is release later today.  </p>
<p>The U.S. market dropped heavily on Thursday when retail sales data grew stronger than expected.</p>
<p>The local market's outperformance after a much weaker than expected domestic employment report faded into distant memory as sell-stops were triggered under the wait of the U.S. decline and the 10-year bond yield here brushed 8.0 percent at one stage.</p>
<p>-- Colin Brinsden 61-2 9373-1800</p>
